# The dev server proxies the API onto its own origin (see vite.config.ts), so
# development talks to a relative base rather than to localhost:8000 directly.
#
# It has to. The app runs at <slug>.localhost:5174 and the API at
# localhost:8000, and those are different SITES to a browser - ports do not
# enter into it - so every cookie the API set was third-party. The refresh
# credential and Django's CSRF token were both withheld from the requests that
# need them, and every page reload ended at "We couldn't restore your session".
#
# Vite loads this only in development, so `npm run build` still reads the real
# API URL from .env. Point the proxy elsewhere with DEV_API_TARGET.
VITE_BACKEND_URL=/v1
